ations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2024-04-11T20:29:48Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":12441367221,"node_id":"SE_lADOAAe_f86FbXUvzwAAAALlkDK1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/events/12441367221","actor":{"login":"kingherc","id":5519665,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTk2NjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5519665?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc","html_url":"https://github.com/kingherc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingherc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2024-04-11T20:29:48Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/2051188329","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/107381#issuecomment-2051188329","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/107381","id":2051188329,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAAe_f856QqZp","user":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTgyODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5058284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner","html_url":"https://github.com/DaveCTurner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-12T07:36:20Z","updated_at":"2024-04-12T07:36:20Z","body":"I believe you're asking about the following line of code, but it would be good if you could confirm this. The other usages of `NoSuchRemoteClusterException` look appropriate to me.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/d920f4f2916929b694930d201793064cbc593877/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/transport/RemoteConnectionManager.java#L154\r\n\r\n> Should we also be returning \"connection exception\" errors for skip_unavailable=true remotes?\r\n\r\nUnclear. The whole point of `skip_unavailable=true` is that we don't even try to establish a connection if one isn't already available and without attempting to establish a connection we won't have a connection exception to report.\r\n\r\n> Should NoSuchRemoteClusterException be reserved for attempts to search clusters that are not configured?\r\n\r\nQuite possibly, although I don't see a perfect alternative today. Maybe a `org.elasticsearch.transport.NodeNotConnectedException` with `discoveryNode = null` and a message that mentions the remote cluster name?\r\n\r\nSuch a change should have no impact on CCR as long as we continue to consider such an exception as retryable (see `org.elasticsearch.xpack.ccr.action.ShardFollowNodeTask#shouldRetry`). I'm concerned that there may be broader impact on CCS tho. @quux00 would you open a PR with your proposed solution, including any changes to CCS to handle it?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/2051188329/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTgyODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5058284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner","html_url":"https://github.com/DaveCTurner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":12445805297,"node_id":"MEE_lADOAAe_f86FbXUvzwAAAALl0-rx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/events/12445805297","actor":{"login":"quux00","id":694387,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDM4Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/694387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","